{"t": 1795095873.1936517, "tool": "analyze", "code": "import numpy as np\nprint(eps.min(), eps.max(), T.min(), T.max(), sigma.min(), sigma.max())\n# fit sigma = a(T) + b(T)*eps^n locally: check curvature in eps for T near 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, 5.5\nfor lo,hi in [(2,2.5),(2.5,3.2),(3.8,4.2),(4.8,5.2),(5.6,6.1)]:\n    m=(T>=lo)&(T<hi)\n    if m.sum()>3:\n        c=np.polyfit(eps[m],sigma[m],2)\n        print(lo,hi,m.sum(), np.round(c,3), np.round(np.std(sigma[m]-np.polyval(c,eps[m])),4))\n", "out": "0.208700930303 4.98849517928 2.015030073 5.99731181424 1.90750877511 21.5903741098\n2 2.5 39 [ 0.44  -2.546  6.04 ] 0.5438\n2.5 3.2 56 [ 0.549 -2.647  7.637] 0.7072\n3.8 4.2 36 [ 0.512 -1.784  9.597] 0.5657\n4.8 5.2 25 [ 0.314  0.093 10.093] 0.5976\n5.6 6.1 20 [ 0.39   0.617 11.526] 0.548\n"}
